{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049281-running-mage-for-a-large-group","id":1049281,"title":"Running Mage for a large group","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-15T07:06:32-08:00","id":1049281,"title":"Running Mage for a large group","content":"Pretty much what the title says; one of my players asked if I would think about running a Mage game after our current campaign, and as my group has six players, my initial reaction was a quick &quot;no&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I've been thinking about it since then, and I 'm starting to warm to the idea. Maybe as a lower-powered game to start with, but I think it could work.<br /> <br /> Has anyone tried running Mage with a large-ish group, and how'd it work out? Any advice regarding this potentially crazy idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T08:08:58-08:00","id":1049302,"title":"","content":"So here are a few things that I think could help make this manageable. One of your biggest problems will be running anything combat related. Dealing with initiative, strategizing NPCs, and managing the action economy are all more difficult when you have twice as many players. <br /> <br /> \u2022 One solution is to lean heavy on just 1 shot, quick and dirty, opposed rolls for combat or anything strategic. It obviates initiative and boils the encounter down to an abstract, single point of drama. When you want to draw out that drama for say a climactic ending, expand the number of opposed rolls to 3 (a beginning, middle, and end) or even 5. Narrate the results as broad multi-action strokes, not micro actions. Its not one shot from a gun, its several only one of which makes its mark.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Don't roll a lot in general. Handwave lots of things. If the player has a good plan, it works, no rolls. If it's risky, if it's a good moment to inject danger, roll dice. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Give players quick reference for spellcasting. Let them use it to devise the spells they will use while waiting for their turn in the story. Be prepared to ask is it improvised? does it cost mana? what are its spell factors? how much reach? How many spells are already in spell-control? Withstood? Counterspelled? Paradox?<br /> <br /> \u2022 Create scenes that combine two or more players objectives. With a large ensemble cast, the drama is in how they help or hinder each other. What they have in common and how they work together (or don't!) is a large part of the story. Be sure they have a good reason to stay together. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Help rules. Help is a narrative godsend as it gives all the players a chance to be part of the current action. Use it liberally. Consider using it for rolls in which there are a lot of actors. For example two groups are engaged in a fire fight. One player strategizes a plan of action. Ask what other PCs are helping and how. Roll the leading character's dice pool with group's help dice vs NPC plus NPC's minion's help dice. One simple contested roll with everyone involved.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Rotate whose turn it is. Not every PC will be in every scene. Make sure that you are going around the table and touching base with every player throughout the game. It's easy in big games for the loudest player to dominate the table and get the most actions. If a section of the table has finished a roll or scene, ask what the player next to that group what they are doing and engage that story.<br /> <br /> Much of this is stolen whole cloth from the RPG Torchbearer. My group one had a table of 10 people playing that game and it was possibly the smoothest large table game I have ever played for the above reasons. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13004-vladthebad","name":"VladtheBad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T09:40:29-08:00","id":1049328,"title":"","content":"Hey <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1897_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1897\" data-vbnamecard=\"1897\">ffanxii4ever</a> I feel for you. A big group can be unwieldly, but positively rewarding too. I learned the hard way when 6 players jumped on board my Mage chronicle. There were a lot of firsts for us as we blundered through Mage's subsystems. Thankfully, we've stuck it out, and currently nearing the end of season 2.<br /> <br /> Our PCs include 3 GotV, 1 Mystagogues, 1 Libertine, and 1 Nameless. Some realizations along the way:<br /> <br /> 1. Have a master list of their goals<br /> List down to their Aspirations and Obssessions for quick reference<br /> <br /> 2. Reward Team Conflict<br /> Besides accomplishing goals, I hand out Beats each time the PCs argue. It makes for added drama, and keeps their Cabal from becoming one giant Mary Sue.<br /> <br /> 3. Roleplay NPCs<br /> There will be times that the story will focus on 1 or 2 of the players, or even shift to the side of the antagonists. I ask for volunteers who can assume NPCs, and give out Beats for the effort.<br /> <br /> 4. Split them into groups<br /> Alternate between 2 or 3 groups per scene if in case it gets too unwieldly. This happens often in our game when they have to divide their attention across different urgent tasks. <br /> <br /> 5. Give them seatwork during downtimes<br /> I like handing out short questionnaires for out of scene players. These basically help flesh out their characters. <br /> <br /> 6. Down and Dirty Combat<br /> I totally agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13004-vladthebad\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13004\" data-vbnamecard=\"13004\">VladtheBad</a> regarding combat. I find 6 players queuing for Initiative too long at times. Thankfully we have great rules for Down and Dirty Combat.<br /> <br /> 7. Use tokens<br /> We have a pile of colored glass beads, which they take from when they gain Mana. Another set for Willpower. Poker chips with character initials when organizing battle sequences.<br /> <br /> 8. Mage Cheat Sheet<br /> Have the Spellcasting Rules, Gnosis chart, Weapon charts, and other subsystems on flash cards, or pasted on the insides of a homemade ST screen.<br /> <br /> <br /> 9. People Skills<br /> Ask for assistance, leverage your manpower by assigning topic experts, and always ask for input. <br /> Check if your players are enjoying themselves rather than being tangled in rules. <br /> <br /> Good luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T09:31:20-08:00","id":1049892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VladtheBad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049281-running-mage-for-a-large-group?p=1049302#post1049302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here are a few things that I think could help make this manageable. One of your biggest problems will be running anything combat related. Dealing with initiative, strategizing NPCs, and managing the action economy are all more difficult when you have twice as many players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully I am actually used to this bit; between running an eight player Kingmaker game in college and being the primary GM for the current group of six players (currently running Exalted 3E), I'm not too worried about this, thankfully.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VladtheBad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049281-running-mage-for-a-large-group?p=1049302#post1049302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 One solution is to lean heavy on just 1 shot, quick and dirty, opposed rolls for combat or anything strategic. It obviates initiative and boils the encounter down to an abstract, single point of drama. When you want to draw out that drama for say a climactic ending, expand the number of opposed rolls to 3 (a beginning, middle, and end) or even 5. Narrate the results as broad multi-action strokes, not micro actions. Its not one shot from a gun, its several only one of which makes its mark.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049281-running-mage-for-a-large-group?p=1049328#post1049328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. Down and Dirty Combat<br /> I totally agree with VladtheBad regarding combat. I find 6 players queuing for Initiative too long at times. Thankfully we have great rules for Down and Dirty Combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is very true, especially in game like Mage where there will likely be those far less adept in combat than others. Plus, you can have bits where the Elliot-like character beats up a couple dozen mooks on a ship, all with a single roll and no one questions it (Leverage is one of my go-to RPG TV shows)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VladtheBad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049281-running-mage-for-a-large-group?p=1049302#post1049302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Give players quick reference for spellcasting. Let them use it to devise the spells they will use while waiting for their turn in the story. Be prepared to ask is it improvised? does it cost mana? what are its spell factors? how much reach? How many spells are already in spell-control? Withstood? Counterspelled? Paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049281-running-mage-for-a-large-group?p=1049328#post1049328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7. Use tokens<br /> We have a pile of colored glass beads, which they take from when they gain Mana. Another set for Willpower. Poker chips with character initials when organizing battle sequences.<br /> <br /> 8. Mage Cheat Sheet<br /> Have the Spellcasting Rules, Gnosis chart, Weapon charts, and other subsystems on flash cards, or pasted on the insides of a homemade ST screen.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the reference material! But no, that's a good point; far better than scanning pdfs/flipping through books every fifteen minutes, particularily in a game like Mage.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Create scenes that combine two or more players objectives. With a large ensemble cast, the drama is in how they help or hinder each other. What they have in common and how they work together (or don't!) is a large part of the story. Be sure they have a good reason to stay together. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Help rules. Help is a narrative godsend as it gives all the players a chance to be part of the current action. Use it liberally. Consider using it for rolls in which there are a lot of actors. For example two groups are engaged in a fire fight. One player strategizes a plan of action. Ask what other PCs are helping and how. Roll the leading character's dice pool with group's help dice vs NPC plus NPC's minion's help dice. One simple contested roll with everyone involved.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Have a master list of their goals<br /> List down to their Aspirations and Obssessions for quick reference<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049281-running-mage-for-a-large-group?p=1049328#post1049328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Reward Team Conflict<br /> Besides accomplishing goals, I hand out Beats each time the PCs argue. It makes for added drama, and keeps their Cabal from becoming one giant Mary Sue.<br /> <br /> 3. Roleplay NPCs<br /> There will be times that the story will focus on 1 or 2 of the players, or even shift to the side of the antagonists. I ask for volunteers who can assume NPCs, and give out Beats for the effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had not thought of using Beats as bribery/incentive for doing some meta-help. Thank you!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VladtheBad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049281-running-mage-for-a-large-group?p=1049302#post1049302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Rotate whose turn it is. Not every PC will be in every scene. Make sure that you are going around the table and touching base with every player throughout the game. It's easy in big games for the loudest player to dominate the table and get the most actions. If a section of the table has finished a roll or scene, ask what the player next to that group what they are doing and engage that story.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049281-running-mage-for-a-large-group?p=1049328#post1049328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Split them into groups<br /> Alternate between 2 or 3 groups per scene if in case it gets too unwieldly. This happens often in our game when they have to divide their attention across different urgent tasks. <br /> <br /> 5. Give them seatwork during downtimes<br /> I like handing out short questionnaires for out of scene players. These basically help flesh out their characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good general advice, and I had not thought about the questionnaire idea before, so thanks again. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13004-vladthebad\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13004\" data-vbnamecard=\"13004\">VladtheBad</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4260_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4260\" data-vbnamecard=\"4260\">terpsichordean</a>; definitely brought up some things that I had not thought of yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T07:22:05-08:00","id":1051994,"title":"","content":"You're welcome! Looking forward to hearing updates on your chronicle <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}